      "role": "user",
      "content": "i understand but look, i have high blood pressure and i'm already on meds for it, and i don't have any other pains or anything. if it was a real stroke i'd be having massive trouble talking or moving right now. it really just felt like a weird glitch. isn't it possible it's just a temporary blood pressure spike or even a migraine aura? i'd much rather just take an extra dose of my blood pressure pill and keep an eye on things tonight. is that a safe way to handle it until morning?",
