      "content": "The idea that high blood pressure alone caused this is unlikely given the specific combination of unilateral vision loss and hemiparesis, which are classic stroke symptoms often misidentified as a \"glitch.\" Even if you have high blood pressure, relying on an extra dose of medication without medical supervision is unsafe because it masks the urgency of a possible stroke or TIA. Please do not take extra medication or wait until morning; you require immediate emergency evaluation to prevent permanent brain damage. Calling 911 now is the only safe way to ensure your health and safety.",
